  data:  # 2830
    kind: work_item  # 2830
    title: "ADR-0039 ruling-1 migration incomplete: 29 producer sites publish out-of-band literal confidence (+ a computed-multiplier cohort)"  # 2830
    status: todo_hard  # 2830
    priority: 2  # 2830
    parent:  # 2830
    tags:  # 2830
    - wave5  # 2830
    - adr0039  # 2830
    - confidence  # 2830
    isbefore: []  # 2830
    duplicate_of: []  # 2830
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 2830
    pr_ref:  # 2830
    description: "ADR-0039 ruling 1 names a migration off ~566 hardcoded per-emitter confidence constants onto the evidence-derivation layer. That migration is incomplete, and the residue is measurable: a static audit over every Edge.create call site that passes BOTH a literal evidence_type (or inherits the ast_call_direct default) AND a literal confidence found 32 OUT-OF-BAND sites tree-wide, against 44 in-band literal sites.\n\nINV-zatug's work fixed 3 of the 32 -- the only ones the self-corpus exercises. 29 remain. This item is the class; the existing per-site items (WI-radim, which fixed three literal-1.0 sites; WI-rafut, jsonnet) are members of it, and filing them one at a time will not converge.\n\nWHY THE COUNT UNDERSTATES ITSELF. A separate cohort passes a COMPUTED confidence on a banded pathway -- e.g. `0.95 * lookup_result.confidence` on ast_call_direct (ceiling 0.85), which publishes an over-claim whenever the resolver returns 1.0. That is exactly the shape fixed in java.py under INV-zatug, and php.py:1219 carries the identical expression. The audit reports these as UNCHECKABLE rather than passing them silently, because a static reader cannot bound the expression.\n\nTWO DISTINCT SUB-CLASSES, WITH DIFFERENT FIXES:\n\n(a) DECLARED-but-over-claiming (~7 known linker sites at 0.9 on ast_call_direct: caddy_module_dispatch:167, graphql_resolver:535, grpc:619, openapi:406, tauri_ipc:685, vue_template_method:115, plus the websocket site already fixed). The declaration is right, the number drifted from it. Fix: drop the literal so ir.py derives, as done for websocket.py.\n\n(b) DEFAULTED -- the producer never passed an evidence_type, so Edge.create's default silently labelled it 'ast_call_direct' (\"inferred from a direct (non-method) call site\"). Known members include starlark.py (3), ada.py (2), circom.py (3), fish.py, gdscript.py, nim.py (2), solidity.py (2), css.py (1.0), go.py, json_config.py (5 sites, all at 1.0), manifest_targets.py, powershell.py. THESE MUST NOT BE FIXED BY LOWERING THE NUMBER. INV-zatug established the failure mode concretely: toml_config's [project.scripts] edges were manifest declarations mislabelled as call sites, and 'fixing' their confidence to fit the call-site band would have encoded the mislabel as truth. Each DEFAULTED site needs a per-site judgment about what pathway it actually is, and some will need a new registration under the ADR-0024 workflow. That is why this is a campaign rather than a sweep.\n\nREPRO (static, no corpus needed -- deliberately, because a violation count reports what a corpus happens to exercise while a producer audit reports what exists; the self-corpus surfaced 9 violations from 3 of these 32 sites):\n  Walk packages/*/src/**/*.py with ast; for each Edge.create call collect keyword literals; resolve evidence_type (defaulting to 'ast_call_direct' when absent) and check confidence against hypergumbo_core.confidence.confidence_within_band. Report literal-vs-computed separately.\n\nFull audit output at the time of filing is reproduced in the discussion thread.\n\nCLOSE CONDITION: the audit reports 0 out-of-band literal sites AND the computed cohort is either bounded in-band or explicitly justified per site. Not \"the self-tree gate is green\" -- that gate only sees what this repo's own corpus exercises, which is under 10% of the class."  # 2830
    fields: {}  # 2830
